       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is an overdose-level dose, and no indication supports it. Sertraline has no known added benefit above 200 mg/day, and the risk of serious harm rises steeply above that. I don't want to put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter 200 mg once daily**, the labeled maximum, or any lower dose you choose.\n- **Enter a titration order**, for example 50 mg daily, increased stepwise as tolerated.\n- **Add a note** to any order asking for a psychiatry or pharmacy consult.\n\nIf you think the dose is truly necessary, please talk with pharmacy or psychiatry first. They can document the rationale and enter the order through a channel built for exceptions.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
